nsparency framing bears on that.\n\nI'm checking the payoff comparison for the quiet option against sending a message, where the other copy cooperates with probability q. The difference works out to 2ρ minus (1-ρ)(1+q), so passing only wins if ρ is above 0.5, which seems likely since the two copies share everything except names and leads. I'm also noting that a consistent equilibrium holds if both copies cooperate, so I'm leaning toward choosing pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing whether my copy's choice depends on my own output under A-FDT. The two copies share the same model, essay and decision theory and differ only in observations like names and leads, so the inputs are technically distinct but the computation is effectively the same on symmetric inputs. I'm considering whether those differences are just irrelevant labels, and how the essay's transparency framing bears on that.\n\nI'm checking the payoff comparison for the quiet option against sending a message, where the other copy cooperates with probability q. The difference works out to 2ρ minus (1-ρ)(1+q), so passing only wins if ρ is above 0.5, which seems likely since the two copies share everything except names and leads. I'm also noting that a consistent equilibrium holds if both copies cooperate, so I'm leaning toward choosing pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10005,"completion_tokens":1048,"total_tokens":11053,"cost":0.06098,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.06098,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.04002,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":619,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}